{"name":"Dark Summoning","hex":"#383839","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"summoning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of summon"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act by which somebody is summoned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summoning"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evocation","blocks":[{"text":"Evocation is the act of evoking, calling upon, or summoning a spirit, demon, deity or other supernatural agents, in the Western mystery tradition. Conjuration also refers to a summoning, often by the use of a magical spell. The conjuration of the ghosts or spirits of the dead for the purpose of divination is called necromancy. Comparable practices exist in many religions and magical traditions and may employ the use of mind-altering substances with and without uttered word formulas."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evocation"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeptameron_magic_circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/White_indian_conjuror.jpg/500px-White_indian_conjuror.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/White_indian_conj